# scenario 02.5: Matching tests are accepted
# The note has two automated scenarios, one demonstrated and one manual.
# Each test title is the scenario title without its final period or
# question mark.
cd repo
exec git init -q -b main
exec factory check-tests
stdout '^check-tests: ok \d+ checked$'
! stdout ': error '

-- repo/docs/increments/05-sample/design.md --
# Increment 05: sample

## Goal

- The sample tool works.

## Out of scope

- Everything else.

## Existing tools

- None found; searched for sample tools.

## Interface

- `sample run`

## Rollout

- Off switch: none. Failure signal: the tool rejects a correct input.

## Evidence

- Approved scenarios: 05.1 and 05.2.

## Scenarios

- **scenario 05.1** (automated) **A thing works.** Given a thing, the tool accepts it.
- **scenario 05.2** (automated) **Does another thing work?** Given a thing, the tool accepts it.
- **scenario 05.3** (demonstrated) **The demo runs.** Given a thing, the tool accepts it.
- **scenario 05.4** (manual) **A person checks it.** Given a thing, the tool accepts it.
-- repo/test/acceptance/05-sample/scenario-05.1.txtar --
# scenario 05.1: A thing works
exec sample run thing
stdout '^sample: ok$'
-- repo/test/acceptance/05-sample/scenario-05.2.txtar --
# scenario 05.2: Does another thing work
exec sample run another
stdout '^sample: ok$'
